From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: IShellWindows list, pending windows, cookies; the desktop's IWebBrowser2 and IShellBrowser (3616)

explorer: IShellWindows list, pending windows, cookies; the desktop's IWebBrowser2 and IShellBrowser

IShellWindows keeps the IDispatch a window registers and now answers Count,
Item, _NewEnum (an IEnumVARIANT over a snapshot), RegisterPending/OnCreated
(a pending window is listed once its object arrives), OnActivated,
ProcessAttachDetach, FindWindowSW with SWFO_COOKIEPASSED, NEEDDISPATCH and
INCLUDEPENDING, and drops windows whose program went away. The class factory
LockServer succeeds. The desktop's IWebBrowser2 answers its documented
properties (name, paths, location, size, ready state, property bag, Refresh
which refreshes the desktop view) and refuses what the desktop cannot do
(navigation, moving, showing); its IShellBrowser answers the browser
callbacks without menus or controls; unknown services give
SVC_E_UNKNOWNSERVICE. Without a taskbar of ours ABM_GETSTATE reports the
always-on-top default. shell32's shelldispatch loses two todo_wine marks.
IWebBrowser2::Document (IShellFolderViewDual) is still open.

Explorer-facing: run the explorer gates at integration.
